{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01Q5AtpoGmscLqZFcPaPUso5","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t{\n2\t \"number\": 63,\n3\t \"title\": \"PDF viewer window.showSaveFilePicker NotAllowedError\",\n4\t \"body\": \"### Preflight Checklist\\n\\n- [x] I have read the [Contributing Guidelines](https://github.com/electron/electron/blob/main/CONTRIBUTING.md) for this project.\\n- [x] I agree to follow the [Code of Conduct](https://github.com/electron/electron/blob/main/CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md) that this project adheres to.\\n- [x] I have searched the [issue tracker](https://www.github.com/electron/electron/issues) for a bug report that matches the one I want to file, without success.\\n\\n### Electron Version\\n\\n43.0.0-alpha.3, 43.4.1, 44.0.0, 45.0.0-alpha.1\\n\\n### What operating system(s) are you using?\\n\\nWindows\\n\\n### Operating System Version\\n\\nWindows 11 Enterprise 23H2\\n\\n### What arch are you using?\\n\\nx64\\n\\n### Last Known Working Electron version\\n\\n43.0.0-alpha.2\\n\\n### Does the issue also appear in Chromium / Google Chrome?\\n\\nNo\\n\\n### Expected Behavior\\n\\nDownloading PDFs with changes should work.\\n\\n### Actual Behavior\\n\\nWhen trying to download a modified PDF \\\"with your changes\\\" the following error is thrown:\\nwindow.showSaveFilePicker failed: NotAllowedError: Failed to execute 'showSaveFilePicker' on 'Window': Third party iframes are not allowed to show a file picker.\\n\\n### Testcase Gist URL\\n\\n_No response_\\n\\n### Additional Information\\n\\nThis bug was already present in earlier electron versions and was fixed, see [issue](`electron/electron#51041`) and [pr](`electron/electron#51042`). The bug is reproducible with the gist of the original issue. \\nWith version 43.0.0-alpha.3 chromium was updated to 150.0.7834.0 [pr](`electron/electron#51609`). In chromium 150.0.7833.0, the logic for IsFilePickerAllowedForCrossOriginSubframe changed, see this [pr](https://github.com/chromium/chromium/commit/3fd5e2cb1ef275dfe83f63d84d604ededba6ccb1).\\nAdditional note: With electron 43.0.0-alpha.2 the save dialog will open, but if the dialog gets closed via cancel or x button, the electron window cannot be closed and the process has to be killed.\",\n5\t \"labels\": [\n6\t  \"43-x-y\",\n7\t  \"44-x-y\",\n8\t  \"45-x-y\",\n9\t  \"bug :beetle:\",\n10\t  \"platform/windows\"\n11\t ],\n12\t \"state\": \"open\",\n13\t \"author_association\": \"NONE\",\n14\t \"as_of\": \"2026-08-28T22:02:21Z\",\n15\t \"replay\": true\n16\t}"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"15669784-5a9d-4b79-82d0-fe3614fffe6b","uuid":"2e9e9ca1-c1d9-47bf-8db5-5e8cd1071a27","timestamp":"2026-10-23T10:02:06.576Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/home/runner/work/cs467-electron-triage/cs467-electron-triage/.triage/issue.json","content":"{\n \"number\": 63,\n \"title\": \"PDF viewer window.showSaveFilePicker NotAllowedError\",\n \"body\": \"### Preflight Checklist\\n\\n- [x] I have read the [Contributing Guidelines](https://github.com/electron/electron/blob/main/CONTRIBUTING.md) for this project.\\n- [x] I agree to follow the [Code of Conduct](https://github.com/electron/electron/blob/main/CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md) that this project adheres to.\\n- [x] I have searched the [issue tracker](https://www.github.com/electron/electron/issues) for a bug report that matches the one I want to file, without success.\\n\\n### Electron Version\\n\\n43.0.0-alpha.3, 43.4.1, 44.0.0, 45.0.0-alpha.1\\n\\n### What operating system(s) are you using?\\n\\nWindows\\n\\n### Operating System Version\\n\\nWindows 11 Enterprise 23H2\\n\\n### What arch are you using?\\n\\nx64\\n\\n### Last Known Working Electron version\\n\\n43.0.0-alpha.2\\n\\n### Does the issue also appear in Chromium / Google Chrome?\\n\\nNo\\n\\n### Expected Behavior\\n\\nDownloading PDFs with changes should work.\\n\\n### Actual Behavior\\n\\nWhen trying to download a modified PDF \\\"with your changes\\\" the following error is thrown:\\nwindow.showSaveFilePicker failed: NotAllowedError: Failed to execute 'showSaveFilePicker' on 'Window': Third party iframes are not allowed to show a file picker.\\n\\n### Testcase Gist URL\\n\\n_No response_\\n\\n### Additional Information\\n\\nThis bug was already present in earlier electron versions and was fixed, see [issue](`electron/electron#51041`) and [pr](`electron/electron#51042`). The bug is reproducible with the gist of the original issue. \\nWith version 43.0.0-alpha.3 chromium was updated to 150.0.7834.0 [pr](`electron/electron#51609`). In chromium 150.0.7833.0, the logic for IsFilePickerAllowedForCrossOriginSubframe changed, see this [pr](https://github.com/chromium/chromium/commit/3fd5e2cb1ef275dfe83f63d84d604ededba6ccb1).\\nAdditional note: With electron 43.0.0-alpha.2 the save dialog will open, but if the dialog gets closed via cancel or x button, the electron window cannot be closed and the process has to be killed.\",\n \"labels\": [\n  \"43-x-y\",\n  \"44-x-y\",\n  \"45-x-y\",\n  \"bug :beetle:\",\n  \"platform/windows\"\n ],\n \"state\": \"open\",\n \"author_association\": \"NONE\",\n \"as_of\": \"2026-08-28T22:02:21Z\",\n \"replay\": true\n}","numLines":16,"startLine":1,"totalLines":16}},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01Q5AtpoGmscLqZFcPaPUso5","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"rule"}}]}
